  "correction_rules": [
    "Model tends to overestimate prices in the short term (1-3 days) after recent spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Mean reversion is strong in the 7-14 day horizon; forecasts should be adjusted downward if prices exceed 1.5 standard deviations above recent mean.",
    "Overshoots after sharp upward moves (e.g., >5% spike) are common; reduce forecast by 10-20% in the next 3-5 days if sentiment remains flat or negative.",
    "When sentiment is consistently 0.00, model should not assume momentum; use 18-day moving average as baseline for 30-day forecast.",
    "Lag error: model often predicts peak 1-2 days too early; delay forecast peak by 1-2 days if recent price action shows consolidation or downward trend.",
    "Horizon-specific: 30-day forecasts are prone to overconfidence in upward trends; apply downward bias of 0.5-1.5% per week if sentiment remains unchanged."
  ]
}
